-- title:
--   Twisted orbital measure is additive Haar in lattice coordinates
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subset L$ be number fields with $[L:K] = 2$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, and let $\delta_0 \in GL_2(L)$, $c \in (L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ and $u \in \mathbb{A}_K^\times$, where $\mathbb{A}_K$ denotes the adele ring of $K$. Write $\delta = \delta_0^{\otimes} \cdot c\,\mathrm{Id}$ for the image of $\delta_0$ under $L \to L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K$ times the scalar matrix $c$. Two hypotheses are imposed: the norm string $\prod_{i=0}^{[L:K]-1} (\sigma_{GL})^{i}(\delta)$, $\sigma_{GL}$ being the automorphism of $GL_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$ induced by $\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id}$, equals the image of the scalar matrix $u\,\mathrm{Id}$ under $\mathbb{A}_K \to L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K$; and $x^{-1}\delta_0\, \sigma(x)$ is never a scalar matrix, for $x \in GL_2(L)$ and scalars in $L^\times$. Fix a finite place $v$ of $K$, i.e. a height one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, let $\delta_v \in GL_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ be the image of $\delta$ under the map induced by $\mathbb{A}_K \to K_v$, and let $T'_v = \{ t : t\,\delta_v\,(\sigma_{GL} t)^{-1} = \delta_v \}$ be the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser of $\delta_v$ in $GL_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$, carrying its Borel structure and a Haar measure $\tau$. Let $b : \iota \to M_2(L)$ be a finite family that is $K$-linearly independent and whose $K$-span is exactly $\{X \in M_2(L) : X\delta_0 = \delta_0\, X^{\sigma}\}$, and for $a \in K_v^{\iota}$ put $A(a) = \sum_k (b_k)^{\otimes a_k}$, the matrix with entries $(b_k)_{ij} \otimes a_k$ summed over $k$. Let $\mu$ be an additive Haar measure on $K_v^{\iota}$ and let $W \subseteq GL_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ be Borel measurable. Writing $\lambda(S) = \int_{S}^{-} \lVert N_{(L \otimes_K K_v)/K_v}(\det t)\rVert \, d\tau(t)$ for the lower Lebesgue integral over a subset $S$ of $T'_v$ of the $\mathrm{ENNReal}$-valued function given by the norm of the $K_v$-algebra norm of the determinant, the conclusion is $$\lambda(\{t : t \in W\}) \cdot \mu(\mathcal{O}_v^{\iota}) = \lambda(\{t : t = A(a) \text{ for some } a \in \mathcal{O}_v^{\iota}\}) \cdot \mu(\{a : A(a) \in W \text{ and } A(a) = t \text{ for some } t \in T'_v\}),$$ where $\mathcal{O}_v$ is the ring of integers of $K_v$.
--
--   This is the local comparison, at a finite place $v$, between the multiplicative measure $\tau$ weighted by $\lVert N(\det)\rVert$ on the twisted centraliser of $\delta_v$ and an additive Haar measure on the twisted commutant read in the linear coordinates $a \mapsto \sum_k b_k \otimes a_k$: the two agree up to the single factor $\lambda(\Lambda)/\mu(\mathcal{O}_v^{\iota})$, here stated as an equality of products so that no normalisation need be chosen. It feeds the local computations of volumes of adelic boxes and of relative indices used in the covolume identities for twisted orbital integrals.
